# =============================================================================
ORACLE value -> oracle.json
#   Differential/quorum on the RETURN value. Most calls return an Array (of numbers and/or
#   strings); toRegex calls return a STRING. strictRanges paths throw -> recorded as {__throw}
#   with constructor name + message (message format is in-envelope, see N1/N3c). Pure function;
#   identical args -> identical output (cache is invisible).

# =============================================================================
SCOPE
#   IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce EXACTLY, all inlined above):
#     - The top-level dispatch (N0..N3d), fillNumbers (N4), fillLetters (N5), and the FULL
#       inlined to-regex-range core + is-number (N6). No external state; deterministic.
#     - The strictRanges RangeError message (util.inspect of [start,end]) and the invalidStep
#       TypeError message are IN-ENVELOPE for codec-faithful (string/number) args:
#         RangeError: "Invalid range arguments: " + util.inspect([start,end])
#           (Node format: ['ab','ef'] -> "[ 'ab', 'ef' ]"; numbers -> "[ 1.5, 5 ]"; null -> "[ null, 5 ]").
#         TypeError:  `Expected step "${step}" to be a number`.
#       (RangeError only triggers when strictRanges is in the 4th/options slot WITH a 3rd/step arg; see N1.)
#   CARRIED DATA: NONE. This is a pure algorithm; no large literal tables.
#   OUT-OF-CONTRACT / OUT-OF-ENVELOPE (genInputs MUST NOT emit these):
#     - options.transform : a FUNCTION value-formatter (replaces the default format in N4/N5).
#       Functions do NOT round-trip the oracle codec, so this path is documented OUT.
#       (Behavior for reference, NOT graded: format(value,index) is called per value; numeric path
#        wraps the result through pad(); letter path uses it raw. e.g. transform=v=>"x"+v on fill(1,5)
#        yields ["x1","x2","x3","x4","x5"].)
#     - step passed as a FUNCTION (3rd arg, node N2) -> re-routed to {transform: step}; same reason, OUT.
#     - Any Symbol-valued or class-instance-valued arg (non-round-trippable) -> OUT.
#     - NaN / +-Infinity numeric args, and `undefined` as an explicit value inside arrays/objects,
#       do not round-trip -> NOT emitted (their reachable behavior is otherwise covered by the
#       finite cases above).

